I added the note #1188 asked for and committed it as 0849fcfa. When a trusted run uses base_url from the project's .yoyo.toml, yoyo now prints one stderr line on every run saying which host the API key goes to. Here it is from a real run whose URL was http://tok:pw@127.0.0.1:9/v1?key=zz:

```
note: requests for custom (with your API key) go to http://127.0.0.1:9, set by base_url in /tmp/bu/p/.yoyo.toml
```

This detects a change, it doesn't prevent one. The first request after a malicious git pull still goes to the new host; the user just sees which host on that same run.

What changed
• The note: trusted_project_base_url_note in src/project_base_url.rs shows only scheme, host and port, filling in the default port if none is given. It never shows a username, password, path, query or fragment. If the URL has no host it can read, the note says so and leaves the value out. The provider name and file path have control characters escaped.
• When it prints: the trust gate now also reports from_trusted_project, and resolve_base_url prints the note only in that case. That covers both places base_url is read: the main path (-p, REPL) and yoyo review. Nothing prints for --base-url or a base_url in the user's own config.
• Policy: it uses the same rules as the existing notice for untrusted runs: yellow, printed even under --quiet (it says where a credential goes), never to stdout. The commit body records this choice.
• New dependency: url is now a direct dependency. It was already in Cargo.lock through reqwest, so nothing new is downloaded.
• Docs: one paragraph in docs/src/troubleshooting/safety.md explains that trust is still per directory and that a changed base_url is named, not re-asked. ARCHITECTURE.md had no entry for this file, so I added one.

Tests
• Unit tests check whole strings: the normal case, a URL with user:pass@ and ?key= showing neither, a URL with no readable host leaving the value out, and control characters escaped. The gate's table test gained rows for trusted, flag-in-trusted-project, user-config and blank values.
• Integration tests (tests/project_base_url_trust.rs, running the built binary): the note appears when trust comes from --trust-project and from the trust store, on both entry points. It is absent for --base-url, user config, and untrusted runs.
• Positive control: I replaced the print with a NEUTERED stub and restored it in one command. Exactly trust_project_flag_uses_the_project_base_url and trust_store_uses_the_project_base_url_on_both_doors went red; the file was restored with no markers left. The "no note" tests stayed green, as they would under any stub, so they only pin the edges.

Checks
• clippy -D warnings, fmt --check and the build all pass.
• cargo test: every result line showed 0 failed. My second, redundant run timed out after 600s, so I have one full pass, not two.
• tests/harness_logic.sh: 396 passed, 1 failed. The failure (projects: with no bot login none are fetched) also fails on the parent commit, so it isn't from this change.

I posted on #1188 with what landed and the open choice: "open: re-ask (pin base_url in the trust store) vs. naming only; my default is to pin, as a later task."
